# Baseline hardening for the static React bundle.
#
# The Worker sets the same headers (plus a request id) on every `/api/*`
# response. HTML, CSS and JS are served straight from the assets binding for
# performance, so they are hardened here instead. `_headers` is part of the
# static-assets contract, which means these rules apply identically in
# `wrangler dev` and in production.
#
# Content-Security-Policy is deliberately left out for now: the SPA ships no
# inline scripts, but enabling CSP safely needs a nonce/hash pipeline and an
# end-to-end review of every asset loader, so it stays a documented follow-up.
#
# Note: `_headers` must not be served as a file itself; Cloudflare consumes it
# at deploy time.
/*
  x-content-type-options: nosniff
  referrer-policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  x-frame-options: SAMEORIGIN
  permissions-policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

/index.html
  cache-control: no-cache

/assets/*
  cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
